# Git Commands Guide for Claude Code

This guide covers essential Git commands used when working with Claude Code for version control and GitHub integration.

## Basic Setup

```bash
# Configure git (one time)
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"

# Check configuration
git config --list
```

---

## Essential Git Commands

### Repository Status

```bash
# Check current status
git status

# See what changed
git diff                          # Unstaged changes
git diff --staged                # Staged changes
git diff HEAD                    # All changes since last commit

# View commit history
git log                          # Full history
git log --oneline               # Compact history
git log -10 --oneline           # Last 10 commits
git log --author="Name"         # Commits by author
```

### Staging and Committing

```bash
# Stage changes
git add .                       # Stage all changes
git add path/to/file           # Stage specific file
git add -p                      # Interactive staging (choose hunks)

# Commit changes
git commit -m "Your message"

# Commit with detailed message (opens editor)
git commit

# Amend last commit (only if NOT pushed)
git commit --amend

# Commit with file changes only (no new files)
git commit -am "message"
```

### Branching

```bash
# View branches
git branch                      # Local branches
git branch -a                   # All branches (local + remote)
git branch -v                   # Branches with last commit

# Create and switch branches
git checkout -b feature/my-feature     # Create and switch
git switch feature/my-feature          # Switch (newer syntax)
git checkout main                      # Switch to main

# Delete branches
git branch -d feature/my-feature          # Local delete
git push origin --delete feature/my-feature  # Remote delete

# Rename branch
git branch -m old-name new-name
```

### Pushing and Pulling

```bash
# Push changes
git push                                    # Push to tracked branch
git push origin feature/my-feature          # Push specific branch
git push -u origin feature/my-feature       # Push and set upstream

# Pull changes
git pull                        # Pull from tracked branch
git pull origin main            # Pull specific branch

# Fetch (without merging)
git fetch
git fetch origin
```

### Undoing Changes

```bash
# Undo unstaged changes
git restore path/to/file
git checkout -- path/to/file    # Older syntax

# Unstage changes
git restore --staged path/to/file
git reset HEAD path/to/file     # Older syntax

# Undo last commit (keep changes)
git reset --soft HEAD~1

# Undo last commit (discard changes)
git reset --hard HEAD~1         # WARNING: Deletes work

# Revert a commit (creates new commit undoing changes)
git revert <commit-hash>
```

### Rebasing (Clean History)

```bash
# Rebase current branch onto main
git rebase main

# Interactive rebase (edit commits)
git rebase -i HEAD~3            # Last 3 commits

# Abort rebase if conflicts
git rebase --abort

# Continue after fixing conflicts
git rebase --continue
```

### Stashing (Temporary Storage)

```bash
# Save work without committing
git stash
git stash save "Work in progress"

# List stashed changes
git stash list

# Apply stash
git stash apply                 # Apply latest
git stash apply stash@{0}       # Apply specific stash

# Pop stash (apply and remove)
git stash pop

# Delete stash
git stash drop
git stash drop stash@{0}
```

