## Common Workflows with Claude Code

### Workflow 1: Feature Development and PR

```bash
# 1. Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/user-authentication

# 2. Make changes (Claude Code edits files)

# 3. Check status before committing
git status
git diff

# 4. Stage and commit
git add .
git commit -m "Add user authentication system"

# 5. Push to remote
git push -u origin feature/user-authentication

# 6. Create PR (using gh cli)
gh pr create --title "Add user authentication" \
  --body "Implements JWT-based authentication"
```

### Workflow 2: Bug Fix and PR

```bash
# 1. Create fix branch from main
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b fix/login-bug

# 2. Make changes

# 3. Commit
git add .
git commit -m "Fix: Resolve login validation bug"

# 4. Push and create PR
git push -u origin fix/login-bug
gh pr create --title "Fix: Login validation" --body "Fixes #456"
```

### Workflow 3: Code Review and Merge

```bash
# 1. Check current branches
git branch -a

# 2. Review PR (using gh)
gh pr view 123
gh pr review 123 --approve

# 3. Merge PR (using gh)
gh pr merge 123 --squash --delete-branch

# 4. Update local main
git checkout main
git pull
```

### Workflow 4: Sync Fork with Upstream

```bash
# 1. Add upstream remote
git remote add upstream https://github.com/original/repo.git

# 2. Fetch upstream changes
git fetch upstream

# 3. Rebase your branch
git checkout your-branch
git rebase upstream/main

# 4. Force push to your fork (only after rebase)
git push -f origin your-branch
```

### Workflow 5: Interactive Rebase Before PR

```bash
# 1. Check your commits
git log main..HEAD --oneline

# 2. Start interactive rebase
git rebase -i main

# 3. In the editor:
# - pick: use commit
# - squash/s: combine with previous
# - reword/r: change commit message
# - drop/d: delete commit

# 4. Fix conflicts if any
git add .
git rebase --continue

# 5. Force push to PR branch
git push -f origin feature/your-feature
```

